From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JalenLin <jalen.lin@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:04:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/22] sound: add the RTD129x audio CPU and the HDMI receiver
 audio

The drivers are kept outside the kernel tree, in kernel/src/acpu, and
copied in by scripts/build-kernel.sh; they carry their own Kconfig
and Makefile. These lines hook that directory in.

Source: https://github.com/JalenLin/BPI-W2-linux

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 sound/Kconfig                             |   2 +
 sound/Makefile                            |   1 +
 sound/realtek-rtd129x-acpu/Kconfig        |  34 +
 sound/realtek-rtd129x-acpu/Makefile       |   9 +
 sound/realtek-rtd129x-acpu/acpu-dp.c      | 636 +++++++++++++++++
 sound/realtek-rtd129x-acpu/acpu-pcm.c     | 497 +++++++++++++
 sound/realtek-rtd129x-acpu/acpu-rpc.c     | 830 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 sound/realtek-rtd129x-acpu/acpu-vo.c      | 567 +++++++++++++++
